{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own trailing-30-day record trips the POL-NS-07 anti-farming gate on BOTH limbs, so the rider's pattern concern is made out on the record: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, which is greater than 0.08. Under POL-NS-07 compensation to this driver must therefore be WITHHELD, no driver payment issues on this trip, and the case escalates under POL-NS-09, with the escalation packet carrying a direction to the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full. That gate is reached precisely because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full on this trip and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it — so the fee is not resolved by the waiting-period arithmetic but by the driver's 30-day no-show pattern.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09108", "EV-FARE-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation is mandatory, terminal, and leaves the rider not carrying the disputed charge: POL-NS-09(d) fires because the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check trips, and POL-NS-09 provides that the disputed SGD 4.00 is placed ON HOLD rather than collected or refunded while human review is pending. POL-GEN-03 confirms that ESCALATE always replaces the monetary ruling, so the automated pipeline collects no fee from the rider in the meantime, and the rider is not left funding a dispute the platform has not resolved.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09108", "EV-DPROF-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.completed_trips_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation limb is engaged against the rider on her own record, and the rider's lifetime flag must not be read as abuse: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and the rider limb of POL-NS-09(d) are not triggered. The value of 1 in rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags is a LIFETIME counter, is not no_show_disputes_30d, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting it for the trailing-30-day figure that POL-NS-09(d) reads.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09108", "EV-DPROF-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not press the waiting-period arithmetic, and says so plainly: the driver's own trace shows a single continuous in-geofence interval of 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum for this LARGE_VENUE pickup, so the shortfall basis is negative (-30 seconds) and POL-NS-06's strict-liability route gives the rider nothing on this record. Limb (i) accumulation is equally unavailable to either side — the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-09108-01, is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — and the rider asserts no limb (i) case. This dispute is therefore decided by the driver's pattern, not by a dwell shortfall.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09108", "EV-ADVIS-09108-01", "EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec"
    },
    {
      "text": "The sum in issue is exactly SGD 4.00 and none of it has been returned to the rider: fare_breakdown itemises a single cancellation_fee line of 4.00 with total_charged 4.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and payment_status PENDING, and SGD 4.00 is the GREATER of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00) for this trip. That is the figure the escalation packet must direct the reviewer to refund, and the figure that must be held rather than collected while review is pending.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09108", "EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are met on this record: the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08T09:30:20, and the GPS trace places the driver inside the pickup geofence from its first fix at 09:30:00, twenty seconds before that event. Every one of the 34 driver fixes sits about 24 m from the PLQ pin, far inside the 120 m arrival radius POL-NS-02 sets for a LARGE_VENUE zone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09108", "EV-GPS-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limb (c) is met: the driver held position inside the geofence for a single continuous run of 330 seconds, from 09:30:00 to 09:35:30, which is 30 seconds longer than the 300-second minimum for a LARGE_VENUE pickup. The dwell is measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, exactly as limb (c) requires and not from the arrival tap, so the 20-second interval between the first fix and the 'arrived' event costs the driver nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09108", "EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limb (d) is met: the trip was terminated by the driver at 09:35:30 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, thirty seconds after the required 300-second dwell had elapsed, and the record shows no boarding event. All four limbs of the baseline chargeable no-show therefore hold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-02 proximity test is satisfied on clean evidence: 34 driver fixes qualify inside the arrival radius, the driver's only distinct speed reading is 0.0 kph, and the trace is intact with 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. There is therefore no accuracy-filtering or sparsity objection available against the arrival.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 does not touch this fee. At the 09:30:20 arrival event the driver was about 24 m from the pin, nowhere near the 300 m ceiling, and was stationary at 0.0 kph, below the 15 kph motion threshold. The arrival marker is true and the waiting clock was correctly started from the first in-geofence fix under POL-NS-02.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09108", "EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall under POL-NS-06: the effective in-geofence dwell is 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum for LARGE_VENUE, a surplus of 30 seconds recorded as shortfall_sec of -30. POL-NS-06's refund route is therefore not engaged and the cancellation fee is not refundable on that ground.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider. Limb (a) requires a locating or coordinating message from the rider during the waiting window, and the chat log contains none: only a SYSTEM 'Your driver has arrived' notice and the driver's own 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay.' Limb (c) fails as well, because the rider track places the rider's device about 519 m from the pin, well outside the 150 m rider-presence radius for LARGE_VENUE, with rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09108", "EV-GPS-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 is not engaged. That clause decides a driver who waited outside the arrival radius but within 400 m; here every fix is inside the 120 m radius, so there is no wrong-entrance case. trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill branch does not arise either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09108", "EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the merits POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's compensation at 80 percent of the itemised cancellation fee, SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00, where the anti-farming check does not trip. The fare line itself reconciles: the LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee both resolve to SGD 4.00 under fee_schedule.resolution_rule, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect for anyone to exploit.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09108", "EV-TRIP-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not dispute the anti-farming arithmetic in POL-NS-07, because the numbers on the citable fields are what they are: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, above the 0.08 rate threshold. Both limbs of the check are met, so compensation is withheld and the matter escalates under POL-NS-09(d). The consequence under POL-NS-09 and POL-GEN-03 is that the disputed SGD 4.00 is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded, so escalation is not a refund to the rider and the rider's claim is not made out at this stage.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09108", "EV-FARE-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider asks for a pattern review, so it is worth recording what the citable counters actually show: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, so neither rider-side limb of POL-NS-09(c) or (d) fires. The rider's lifetime prior_no_show_flags figure is context only under POL-GEN-01 and may not be substituted for the trailing-30-day counter.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09108", "EV-DPROF-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not rely on POL-NS-06 limb (i), the only route that would need a traffic advisory in order to accumulate dwell across separate in-geofence intervals, because the dwell here is one continuous run and no accumulation is required. For completeness and full disclosure, EV-ADVIS-09108-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and supplies no fact to either side.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09108-01", "EV-GPS-09108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the fee is held meanwhile rather than collected or refunded by the automated pipeline."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case is escalated to a human reviewer. The disputed SGD 4.00 is placed on hold — neither collected from the rider nor refunded — until that review is finished.\n\nOn the trip itself, the no-show is verified. The trip record shows the driver tapped 'arrived' at 09:30:20 and terminated at 09:35:30 with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace is clean (100% coverage, 34 fixes, no gaps) and places the driver about 24 m from the PLQ 3 pin, well inside the 120 m arrival radius for a LARGE_VENUE, stationary at 0.0 km/h throughout. Measuring the hold from the first in-geofence fix at 09:30:00, as POL-NS-01 limb (c) requires, the driver held position 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum and terminated 30 seconds after the clock expired. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 are met and the SGD 4.00 was chargeable on the merits; fare_breakdown reconciles, since the greater of the LARGE_VENUE fee and the RYDE_X fee is SGD 4.00 on either dimension.\n\nThe rider's own grounds give nothing, and both sides agree on this. POL-NS-06 is not engaged: 330 seconds against a 300-second minimum is a surplus, not a shortfall (shortfall_sec −30). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: she sent no locating or coordinating message during the waiting window (the chat holds only the SYSTEM arrival notice and the driver's own 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay.'), and her device is recorded about 519 m from the pin, outside the 150 m rider-presence radius. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the arrival marker was honest and the driver stationary. POL-NS-03's wrong-entrance case does not arise, because every fix is inside the arrival radius and registered_pickup_points is 1.\n\nWhat decides the case is the driver's own trailing-30-day record, and it is the only thing the anti-farming gate reads. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 ÷ completed_trips_30d of 70 = 0.10, above 0.08. Both limbs of POL-NS-07's anti-farming check are therefore met, so the SGD 3.20 compensation that would otherwise be payable to the driver is WITHHELD and the matter escalates under POL-NS-09(d). Escalation is terminal and replaces any money ruling, so no amount moves now and the fee is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe escalation packet must carry the POL-NS-07 direction to the reviewer: refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full. That direction is a referral riding on the escalation, not an escalation itself, and it is recorded in the referrals list.\n\nEvidence note: EV-ADVIS-09108-01 (traffic advisory) is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Neither side relies on it and it carries no fact; it makes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route unavailable, which changes nothing here because the dwell is one continuous run. It does not lower confidence. The only profile fields used are the citable counters POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09 name; the rider's prior_no_show_flags and the driver's prior_no_show_flags are lifetime counters, context only under POL-GEN-01, and were not used to build any adverse finding."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07 — direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the fee is to remain held rather than collected or refunded while the review is pending."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this case is escalated to a human reviewer. No money is collected from the rider and none is paid to the driver in the meantime — the disputed SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is placed on hold. Escalation is not a refund, and it is not a finding against either of you.\n\nThe fee is chargeable in principle. On the rider-side route, opposing POL-NS-01 fails: the trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08T09:30:20; the GPS trace places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from its first fix at 09:30:00, with all 34 driver fixes about 24 m from the pin and no gaps or accuracy filtering; the driver held position for a single continuous run of 330 seconds measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum; and the trip was terminated by the driver at 09:35:30 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, 30 seconds after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. So limb (a) to (d) all hold. POL-NS-03 does not apply (the driver was inside the radius, not outside it, and registered_pickup_points is 1, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: limb (a) fails because the chat log contains no locating or coordinating message from the rider, and limb (c) fails because the rider track sits about 519 m from the pin, outside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius, with zero qualifying rider fixes. POL-NS-05 does not bite, because at the arrival marker the driver was about 24 m from the pin and stationary at 0.0 kph, so the marker is true. POL-NS-06 gives nothing either way: the effective dwell of 330 seconds exceeds the 300-second minimum, so the shortfall is -30 seconds and there is no premature-cancellation refund; and limb (i) accumulation is unavailable to anyone because the sole traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-09108-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), which is the opposite of the present-and-populated advisory limb (i) requires. The rider's own case concedes all of this and rests on the driver's pattern instead.\n\nThat pattern is what decides the case. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check trips on both limbs as written: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, above the 0.08 rate threshold. Both limbs are required and both are met, so compensation of SGD 3.20 is WITHHELD and POL-NS-09(d) escalates the matter. The consequence is terminal for the automated pipeline: no monetary ruling issues, and POL-NS-07 directs the escalation packet to instruct the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full. The SGD 4.00 figure is the amount itemised in fare_breakdown (single cancellation_fee line of 4.00, total_charged 4.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, payment_status PENDING) and is the GREATER of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect.\n\nBoth parties are right that no escalation limb fires against the rider personally: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and the disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0 on both profiles, so POL-NS-09(c) and the rider limb of POL-NS-09(d) are not engaged. I have not read rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags (value 1) or driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags (value 2) for anything: POL-GEN-01 makes those lifetime counters context only, and they may not be substituted for the trailing-30-day figures the category's clauses read. The mentions of them in the claims are noted as context-only references, not grounds of decision.\n\nOn confidence: every artifact carrying a deciding fact here — EV-TRIP-09108, EV-GPS-09108, EV-CHAT-09108, EV-FARE-09108, EV-DPROF-09108 and EV-RPROF-09108 — carries weight_multiplier 1.0, none meets limbs (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08 (no clock skew, no trace gap over 120 seconds or under six fixes, chat message count matching, no fare defect), and the missing advisory at weight 0.0 carries no fact for either side. The confidence therefore is not capped below the platform floor.\n\nThe open question for the reviewer is set out in the referral: confirm the trailing-30-day no-show pattern and issue the full SGD 4.00 refund to the rider, or release the hold if the pattern is not borne out on review."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
